BD Law Assistant (RAG-Based Legal AI System) System Design Document

1. Introduction
BD Law Assistant is an AI-powered legal research and assistance platform tailored for Bangladesh. Leveraging Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with state-of-the-art LLMs, the system delivers contextually accurate, Bengali-language legal guidance, reduces manual research overhead, and democratizes access to statutes, case laws, and legal interpretations.
Objectives:
Provide rapid, accurate answers to legal queries in Bengali
Enable laypersons and professionals to access authoritative legal information
Streamline ingestion and retrieval of legal documents using vector search
Support conversational follow-up queries via chatbot interface

2. System Architecture Overview
[React Frontend]
       ↓ REST API
[API Gateway (Spring Boot)]
       ↓ gRPC/REST
[Python RAG Microservice]
   ↕           ↕
[LangChain Module]    [Vector Store (FAISS/Pinecone/Weaviate)]
       ↕
[PostgreSQL (metadata)]
[Document Storage (AWS S3)]

[Go Service - Background Tasks & Concurrency]
Components:
Frontend: React SPA with search bar & chat UI
API Gateway: Java Spring Boot for auth, routing, logging
RAG Microservice: Python service orchestrating embedding, retrieval, generation
Vector Store: High-performance semantic index of text chunks
Data Storage: PostgreSQL for metadata, S3 for raw documents
Go Service: Concurrent background processing (ingestion, indexing, monitoring)

3. Component Design
3.1 Frontend (React.js)
Modules: SearchBar, ChatWindow, QueryHistory
Interaction: Issues REST calls to API Gateway
State Management: Redux for user session, query context
Styling: Tailwind CSS for responsive design
3.2 API Gateway (Java Spring Boot)
Responsibilities:
User authentication & authorization (JWT)
Rate limiting & request validation
Routing to RAG Microservice or auxiliary services
Centralized logging & metrics (Prometheus)
Endpoints:
POST /api/v1/query → handle user questions
GET /api/v1/history → fetch past queries
POST /api/v1/documents → upload new legal docs
3.3 RAG Microservice (Python 3.10+)
Framework: FastAPI or Flask
Core Logic: LangChain pipeline
Embedder: OpenAIEmbeddings or SentenceTransformer
Retriever: Vector store query (top-k chunks)
Generator: LLM prompt with retrieved context → produce answer
Endpoints:
POST /rag/query → returns answer + source snippets
POST /rag/ingest → ingest new docs (trigger chunking & embedding)
3.4 Vector Store
Options: FAISS (on‑prem), Pinecone or Weaviate (managed)
Data Model: Stores vectors with metadata (doc_id, chunk_id, text)
Access Pattern: kNN search to retrieve relevant chunks
3.5 Data Storage
PostgreSQL:
Tables: users, queries, documents, chunks
Stores metadata and audit logs
AWS S3:
Raw document files (PDF, DOCX)
Versioning enabled
3.6 Go Service
Use Cases:
Ingestion Workers: Concurrent download/cleanup of documents
Index Updater: Batch or streaming embedding & vector DB update
Monitoring: Health checks, queue status
Patterns: Goroutines + Channels for worker pools
Integration: Message queue (RabbitMQ/Redis) for job dispatch

4. Data Flow
Document Ingestion: Admin uploads PDF → API Gateway → Go Service enqueues ingest job → Python RAG service chunks & embeds → Vector Store & metadata updated
User Query: Frontend sends question → API Gateway routes to RAG service → Retriever fetches top-k chunks → Generator produces answer → Gateway returns response with citations
Follow-up: Chat context passed to RAG pipeline for multi-turn interactions

5. Non‑Functional Requirements
Scalability: Kubernetes deployment with autoscaling for microservices
Performance: <500ms for retrieval, <2s for generation
Security: TLS everywhere, OAuth2/JWT, role‑based access
Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, ELK stack for logs & metrics

6. Deployment Architecture
Containers: Docker images for each service
Orchestration: Kubernetes (EKS/GKE/AKS)
CI/CD: GitHub Actions pipelines for build, test, deploy
Secrets: AWS Secrets Manager / Kubernetes secrets

